  "name": "Create Instagram, TikTok and LinkedIn carousels from a form with GPT Image and PostWire",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "2af48080-8f57-42be-a55f-8a7584252cba",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -636,
        -97
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 520,
        "height": 742,
        "content": "## Create carousels with GPT Image and post them\nType a topic in a form and get a finished carousel. OpenAI plans the slides, GPT Image draws them, and PostWire posts them as an Instagram carousel, a TikTok photo post and a LinkedIn multi-image post.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Carousel brief** is an n8n form: topic, audience, number of slides and networks.\n2. **Plan the carousel with OpenAI** returns one headline, image prompt and alt text per slide, plus the captions for each network.\n3. Each slide gets a PostWire upload slot, **GPT Image** draws it (portrait 2:3 is too tall for Instagram, so slides are square) and the file goes straight to the slot: no Drive, no public link.\n4. **Collect the slides** puts the links back in order with their alt text, and **Publish the carousel** posts them to every network. The form submission is the idempotency key, so a retry never posts twice.\n5. Every carousel is logged in Google Sheets with its links; when a network refuses, **Gmail** emails you the fix.\n\n### Setup\n1. Create a free account at postwire.io, connect your networks and copy your API key. In n8n add a **Header Auth** credential (name `Authorization`, value `Bearer pw_live_\u2026`) and select it in the three PostWire nodes.\n2. Add an OpenAI credential (about one cent per slide with gpt-image-1-mini).\n3. Create a sheet with the columns date, topic, slides, status, links and note, and pick it in both Sheets nodes. Connect Gmail and put your address in **Email me the fix**.\n4. Open the form URL from **Carousel brief** and send a topic.\n\n### Customize\nChange the visual style in the OpenAI system message."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
